  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 219 PM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nGlobal model guidance diverges considerably early to mid-next week \nin the evolution of an upper-level trough that propagates into the \ncentral CONUS Monday into Tuesday as the Omega Block breaks down. \nThe track, amplitude, and tilt of this trough vary across guidance \nincluding whether an associated cold front passes through the CWA \nTuesday or early Wednesday, enters and then stalls in the CWA, or \nstalls before reaching the CWA altogether. Accordingly, the NBM \ninterquartile range increases to between 7 and 15 F Tuesday onward, \nwith the 75th percentile remaining steady and the 25th percentile \ncooling closer to average. If the front reaches the CWA, showers \nwill also become possible, with greatest probabilities of measurable \nrainfall in global ensemble models across central/northeastern MO \nand west-central IL at 30 to 50 percent. However, a widespread, \nsubstantial rainfall appears unlikely in the ranges of current \nscenarios. The aforementioned uncertainties persist through the end \nof the forecast period, late next week.",
